WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:06.212
Monday was Show-and-Tell Day in Brandy's class.

2
00:00:06.213 --> 00:00:10.774
Each week five students brought something to class.

3
00:00:10.775 --> 00:00:15.187
They showed it to their classmates and told them about it.

4
00:00:15.188 --> 00:00:19.983
"My turn is next week," Brandy thought nervously.

5
00:00:19.984 --> 00:00:23.860
Last Monday Kara brought her iguana.

6
00:00:23.861 --> 00:00:28.928
The week before, Miyuki performed a magic trick.

7
00:00:28.929 --> 00:00:36.604
"I don't have any pets or hobbies," Brandy thought. "What can I show?"

8
00:00:36.605 --> 00:00:41.399
That weekend Brandy was quiet.

9
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:46.775
"Is something wrong?" Mom asked.

10
00:00:46.776 --> 00:00:51.928
"What should I do for show-and-tell on Monday?" Brandy asked.

11
00:00:51.929 --> 00:00:58.081
"Hmm," Mom said. "You're good at many things."

12
00:00:58.082 --> 00:01:01.315
"Like what?" Brandy asked.

13
00:01:01.316 --> 00:01:07.056
"Like math and . . ." Mom pointed to a shelf.

14
00:01:07.057 --> 00:01:11.188
"Can you please get that jar for me?"

15
00:01:11.189 --> 00:01:16.158
"Sure!" Brandy was always ready to help Mom.

16
00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:20.205
Three years ago Mom was in a car accident.

17
00:01:20.206 --> 00:01:23.154
Now she used a wheelchair.

18
00:01:23.155 --> 00:01:25.975
Mom could do a lot for herself.

19
00:01:25.976 --> 00:01:30.640
But sometimes she needed Brandy's help.

20
00:01:30.641 --> 00:01:33.850
Brandy handed Mom the jar.

21
00:01:33.851 --> 00:01:38.220
"Thanks," Mom said. "Back to show-and-tell . . ."

22
00:01:38.221 --> 00:01:42.796
She reminded Brandy of some things Brandy liked to do.

23
00:01:42.797 --> 00:01:46.687
Brandy did enjoy drawing and playing soccer.

24
00:01:46.688 --> 00:01:55.456
But nothing felt quite right for show-and-tell . . . until Sunday night!

25
00:01:55.457 --> 00:01:59.936
In school the next day, Brandy felt worried.

26
00:01:59.937 --> 00:02:04.941
When it was time for show-and-tell, she looked nervously at the door.

27
00:02:04.942 --> 00:02:09.535
"I hope this was a good idea," she thought.

28
00:02:09.536 --> 00:02:14.072
"It's your turn, Brandy," Mr. Francesco said.

29
00:02:14.073 --> 00:02:20.644
She looked at the door again. "I, um, maybe—"

30
00:02:20.645 --> 00:02:29.234
"Hello!" The door opened. "Sorry I'm late!" Brandy's mom said.

31
00:02:29.235 --> 00:02:36.376
"Phew!" Brandy thought. She joined Mom near Mr. Francesco's desk.

32
00:02:36.377 --> 00:02:40.700
"I'm going to talk about my mom today," Brandy said.

33
00:02:40.701 --> 00:02:45.094
"As you can see, she uses a very cool wheelchair.

34
00:02:45.095 --> 00:02:48.762
There are lots of things she can do with it."

35
00:02:48.763 --> 00:02:56.196
Brandy's mom demonstrated going forward and backward. Then she did a spin.

36
00:02:56.197 --> 00:02:59.005
The class clapped.

37
00:02:59.006 --> 00:03:04.773
"The wheelchair makes her life much easier," Brandy said.

38
00:03:04.774 --> 00:03:10.186
"Something else makes my life easier." Mom beamed at Brandy.

39
00:03:10.187 --> 00:03:13.864
"My daughter helps me all the time!"

40
00:03:13.865 --> 00:03:20.386
The class started clapping again. This time it was for Brandy.

41
00:03:20.387 --> 00:03:25.419
"What an interesting show-and-tell!" Mr. Francesco said.

42
00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:28.850
"Brandy, that was a wonderful idea!"

43
00:03:28.851 --> 00:03:34.835
Brandy grinned and then hugged Mom.

